Meowderator — Privacy Policy
Last updated: 25. nov. 2026
Terms of Service · Privacy Policy
• Meowderator only stores what it needs to run its features in your server.
• I never sell your data, never use it for ads and never use it to train AI.
• Most data belongs to a server's setup. Remove the bot, and that server's data is deleted within 30 days.
• It's a free bot run by one person, so data requests are only handled as far as the law requires (see section 8).
The full policy below is what actually applies; this box is just the gist.
1. Who runs Meowderator
Meowderator is run by its developer ("I", "me"), who is responsible for the data it handles (the "data controller" under laws like the GDPR). This policy explains what the bot collects, why, and what you can do about it. It goes together with the Terms of Service.
Server admins choose which features are turned on in their server, which decides what data the bot handles there.
