3. What the bot doesn't collect
• No passwords, Discord tokens or login details.
• No payment or card details (Meowderator is free).
• No IP addresses, location or device info. Discord doesn't give bots this.
• No DMs, except messages you send directly to the bot.
• Nothing from servers the bot isn't in.
4. How the data is used
Data is used only to:
• run the bot's features in the servers that added it;
• keep servers safe (automod, anti-nuke, anti-raid, blacklists);
• fix bugs, stop abuse and keep the bot running;
• follow the law.
It's never sold, used for ads, used to build profiles of you, or used to train AI.
Legal basis (for the EU, EEA and UK):
• Legitimate interests: running the features a server has chosen, and keeping servers and the bot safe from abuse.
• Contract: providing the Service under the Terms of Service.
• Legal obligation: when the law requires it.
5. Who the data is shared with
I never sell or rent data. It's only shared with:
• Discord, because the bot runs on Discord and everything goes through it.
• My hosting provider, which stores the bot's database on its servers.
• Roblox, only when you use Roblox features, to look up public profiles.
• Authorities, only when the law requires it, or to protect the Service, users or the public from serious harm.
• A new owner, if the bot is ever handed over. This policy keeps applying to your data.
Data may be stored or processed outside your country. Where the law requires it, I use proper safeguards for those transfers.
Anything the bot posts in a server (logs, cards, moderation messages) can be seen by that server's members based on its channel permissions. The server controls that, not me.
