7. Security
I take reasonable steps to protect the data, such as limiting who can reach the database and keeping the bot's token secret. But no system is completely secure, and I can't promise yours will never be exposed.
To the maximum extent permitted by law, I'm not responsible for breaches caused by things outside my control, such as attacks on Discord, my host or other third parties. If a breach puts your rights at real risk, I'll tell you as the law requires.
8. Your rights
Meowderator is free and run by one person, so I only handle data requests where the law requires me to. Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in the EU, EEA or UK), the law gives you some rights over your data that no terms can remove. You can:
• get a copy of the data the bot holds about you;
• have wrong data corrected;
• have your data deleted;
• object to, or limit, how it's used;
• get your data in a portable format;
• complain to your local data protection authority.
How requests work:
• Requests are only accepted through [SUPPORT SERVER LINK]. DMs, pings and anything else are ignored.
• You must prove the Discord account is yours.
• You only get data about yourself. Server data, other people's data, and records that would affect other people's rights are never handed out.
• Requests that are clearly unfounded, repeated or excessive are refused, as the law allows.
• I answer within the time the law requires, normally one month.
Some data may be kept after a deletion request when there's a good reason, such as a blacklist entry to stop abuse, or a moderation record a server needs for its safety. Deleting your data may also mean some features stop working for you.
9. Children
Meowderator isn't meant for anyone under 13, or under Discord's minimum age in their country. I don't knowingly collect data from children below that age. If you think a child's data is stored, ask for it to be deleted as described in section 8.
10. Changes
I can update this policy at any time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows the newest version, and big changes will be announced in the support server. The updated policy applies from the day it's posted.
